{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276791-ritual-questions","id":1276791,"title":"Ritual questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-26T07:47:29-08:00","id":1276791,"title":"Ritual questions","content":"I have some questions regarding rituals casting in M20<br /> <br /> 1- The hermetic tradition book has a sidebar about prep time, where it says that a hermetic could make all the casting but the very end, safely in his home just to unleash the spell by completing that missing part in a stressful situation. It even compares to an akashic doing the meditation in his temple or etherite building his machine in his lab. Is the Arete rolled during the incomplete casting in his home or on the field, by completing the spell?<br /> Also, can he do this with rituals?<br /> <br /> 2- What is the difference between a ritual and &quot;picking up where you left off&quot;? As I understand, rituals have a fixed diff that only raises if you fail a roll and want to continue, but takes a lot of time. While the &quot;picking up&quot; raises diff even when the roll succeded but takes just as many turns as you roll to complete, meaning that shouldn't take more than some minutes. Both can be rolled indefinitely (unless you botch twice), but will build up paradox for every roll. Is that it?<br /> <br /> 3- Is it possible to make a trinket or charm (or any wonder) with extended rolls, like rituals? If a mage wants to make a very potent healing potion, for example, one that would heal all 7 vitality points, how it could be made?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T08:45:21-08:00","id":1276802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276791-ritual-questions#post1276791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some questions regarding rituals casting in M20<br /> <br /> 1- The hermetic tradition book has a sidebar about prep time, where it says that a hermetic could make all the casting but the very end, safely in his home just to unleash the spell by completing that missing part in a stressful situation. It even compares to an akashic doing the meditation in his temple or etherite building his machine in his lab. Is the Arete rolled during the incomplete casting in his home or on the field, by completing the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Arete is rolled at the moment of completing the Effect, not during the preparations. Otherwise this would be identical to using Time 4 to store / hang a Spell for later use.<br /> Also, it doesn't have to be a 'missing part' that is completed ; it could be an additional element to the Spell that casts the Magick when it is done. Maybe this is ( or sounds ) identical in practice, but I dislike 'missing part' as a term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-26-2018, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T10:28:06-08:00","id":1276821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3- Is it possible to make a trinket or charm (or any wonder) with extended rolls, like rituals? If a mage wants to make a very potent healing potion, for example, one that would heal all 7 vitality points, how it could be made?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rituals it's usually the way you make trinkets and charms. Both tend to require a notable amount of successes, if only for the Duration<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2- What is the difference between a ritual and &quot;picking up where you left off&quot;? As I understand, rituals have a fixed diff that only raises if you fail a roll and want to continue, but takes a lot of time. While the &quot;picking up&quot; raises diff even when the roll succeded but takes just as many turns as you roll to complete, meaning that shouldn't take more than some minutes. Both can be rolled indefinitely (unless you botch twice), but will build up paradox for every roll. Is that it? </div> </div> </div>You're mostly right.<br /> <br /> Only Rituals build Paradox for every roll (and this Pradox only becomes a problem if you Botch, otherwise it's ignored).<br /> <br /> There's a maximum amount of rolls you can make equal to Arete + Willpower (i.e 8 rolls for someone with Arete 2, Willpower 6). The amount of successes you can get isn't limited but it's never going to be infinite.<br /> This rule it's for Rituals, and thus theoretically &quot;picking up where you left off&quot; can be repeated indefinitely but the dificulty raise makes it unlikely to work so far as to ever reach the maximum power you can get from your Rituals (there's no picking up if you Botch a roll, and as the difficulty increases gathering successses becomes less likely)<br /> <br /> Usually you need Ritual rules to include things like &quot;working in concert&quot; and the Cult background, as these aren't part of the normal casting rules either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1- The hermetic tradition book has a sidebar about prep time, where it says that a hermetic could make all the casting but the very end, safely in his home just to unleash the spell by completing that missing part in a stressful situation. It even compares to an akashic doing the meditation in his temple or etherite building his machine in his lab. Is the Arete rolled during the incomplete casting in his home or on the field, by completing the spell? </div> </div> </div>If you read very carefully you will notice that this rule talks about Focus, it has nothing to do with Rituals or Arete in the OOC sense.<br /> <br /> The rule exists in order to fasten Focus usage: A Hermetic won't be able to fight with magick if he needs to stop and chant one hour each time he wants to launch a fireball, like High Ritual demands.<br /> <br /> The rule states that, much like an Etherite builds his Raygun in his lab , a Hermetic can prepare a fireball by starting to chant the 10 names of Michael but stoping at the 9th. This doesn't imply any Arete roll, it's just you preparing your Instrument just like the Etherite of the example, so your Instrument it's ready when the vampire shows up and you have only precious seconds to fire your Forces 3/Prime 2 blast<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, can he do this with rituals? </div> </div> </div>No, he can't","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T11:35:19-08:00","id":1276837,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers. <br /> <br /> 2- Do &quot;picking up&quot; get +1 even in &quot;successful&quot; rolls as in there were successes but not enough yet? <br /> And in extended rolls (both rituals or picking up) can the effect begin to work before completion? For example, if a mage wants ro buff his stamina from 2 to 5 for a turn and rolls 2 successes in round 1 and 1 success in round 2, does his stamina gets to 4 in round 1 and 5 in round 2, or it stays at 2 and is buffed to 5 when the effect is completed in round 2? <br /> <br /> 3- I see. In this case, if the mage wants such a potion, how could he do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T06:34:38-08:00","id":1276986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276791-ritual-questions?p=1276837#post1276837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers.<br /> 2- Do &quot;picking up&quot; get +1 even in &quot;successful&quot; rolls as in there were successes but not enough yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. They're considered &quot;failures&quot; because in a sense they are: you've not managed to get enough successes as you need yet. The good thing it's that you don't get an <i>aditional</i> +1 if you fail - geting 0 successes is a +1 like with any other number of successes. Only Botches are bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And in extended rolls (both rituals or picking up) can the effect begin to work before completion? For example, if a mage wants ro buff his stamina from 2 to 5 for a turn and rolls 2 successes in round 1 and 1 success in round 2, does his stamina gets to 4 in round 1 and 5 in round 2, or it stays at 2 and is buffed to 5 when the effect is completed in round 2? </div> </div> </div>No. The effect it's cast when the roll ends. Visually you could represent it as energy building up or muscles bulking, but system wise you can't get benefit until you complete the casting<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3- I see. In this case, if the mage wants such a potion, how could he do it? </div> </div> </div>Life 3/Prime 3, it's a Charm (a one use Wonder, you can craft batches of these). You can do that as per the Wonder creation rules of M20 (The Toybox chapter). There are expanded rules in BoS. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T06:56:02-08:00","id":1276989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276791-ritual-questions?p=1276986#post1276986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. The effect it's cast when the roll ends. Visually you could represent it as energy building up or muscles bulking, but system wise you can't get benefit until you complete the casting</div> </div> </div> </div> I see. And in the case of the mage casting the +2 strenght and later wanting to get +1 (+3 total)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276791-ritual-questions?p=1276986#post1276986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life 3/Prime 3, it's a Charm (a one use Wonder, you can craft batches of these). You can do that as per the Wonder creation rules of M20 (The Toybox chapter). There are expanded rules in BoS. </div> </div> </div> </div>But this way the wonder would heal according to the Arete rolled when used. There is no way of accumulating rolls or fixating at 7 health levels? I guess only with Time 4 trigger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T08:04:52-08:00","id":1277005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I see. And in the case of the mage casting the +2 strenght and later wanting to get +1 (+3 total)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most effects don't stack. If you have +2 to Strenght, in order to get +3 you need to gather the same amount of successes you would need if you had +0.<br /> <br /> The other spell doesn't get &quot;enhanced&quot;, it's mostly ignored by the new magick and you get to keep the highest bonus of the two. However the lowest isn't dispelled, it just doesn't have any notable effect: If the +3 lasted a scene and the +2 lasted a year, your mage would have a +3 for the scene and return to the +2 when the scene ends.<br /> <br /> The only exception it's that bonuses are canceled by penalties and vice versa.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But this way the wonder would heal according to the Arete rolled when used. There is no way of accumulating rolls or fixating at 7 health levels? I guess only with Time 4 trigger? </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting question that's a rather complex issue.<br /> <br /> If you use just the basic rules of M20 then yes, it's like you say. However if you use the expanded rules (that are based on the older rules) it gets more complicated.<br /> <br /> Most Gadgets aren't rolled at all, it's not only that they don't have Arete, the examples given in the book doesn't depend on Arete at all and can be used by mortals. They just work. How this works isn't realy clarified in any edition.<br /> <br /> My interpretation it's that you roll at the moment of the ritual to create the Wonder and the successes gathered are what's going to constitute the effect. A lot like Time 4, except that you need to expend Quintessence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-27-2018, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T16:21:53-08:00","id":1277112,"title":"","content":"Reading the M20 Book of Secrets, I realized that, as Talismans/Fetiches have they own Arete/Gnosis and Artifacts uses the mage's Arete, the roll i always made when activating the wonder. Trinckets require the mage to roll twice the successes necessary to cast the effect, on the Arete roll during creation. They just forgot about the Charms .<br /> <br /> So, I guess this rule could be used in Charms/Gadgets. In this case, a potion that heals 8 levels of damage would require 8 successes on the Arete roll during creation.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> I was wondering, how could a mage put trap spells, like a rune on the floor to paralyze or shock an enemy, or a protection spell like Dr. Strange casted on the Eye of Agamoto n the Avengers movie, without Time 4 or making wonders? Isn't Time 4 too much for such a simple effect?<br /> <br /> I guess this question could go in this thread as well:<br /> <br /> 4- M20 has rules for damage over time. HDYDT pg.37 &quot;Walls, Floods, Force-Fields, Etc&quot; has an example where a wall of ice requires 6 successes to deal 6 levels of damage to anyone who touches it, for the entire day (3 suc for duration +3 for damage). Following this logic and the Mage rule where you can heal using the damage chart in the proportion of 2 health levels per success, then a mage can heal 6 levels of damage everytime someone hurts him, for an entire day with 6 successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 12-27-2018, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T11:18:21-08:00","id":1277230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276791-ritual-questions?p=1277112#post1277112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering, how could a mage put trap spells, like a rune on the floor to paralyze or shock an enemy, or a protection spell like Dr. Strange casted on the Eye of Agamoto n the Avengers movie, without Time 4 or making wonders? Isn't Time 4 too much for such a simple effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>For your simple but quite unbreakable spells you want the Minor Wards (Correspondence 2+/ Other Spheres) from HDYDT:<br /> <br /> Minor Wards cannot really block anything but they can hold other spells that are automagically triggered when someone crosses the barrier.<br /> <br /> Wards that aren't set on a location but on an object or person have to be &quot;locked&quot; there with the appropiate Pattern Sphere. The level of Correspondence needed it's either equal to the highest Sphere level used in the Ward or 2, whatever it's higher (Similar as when you use Corr to cast at distance).<br /> <br /> A given example it's a Life 3/ Mind 3 effect that gives trespassers a psychic shock when they try to pass the ward. Overt attacks like this one work only once per point of Quintessence expended in the Ritual to create the Ward (and are triggered only once per trespass), but more subtle influences that are always active within the ward (like a house that frigthens trespassers) may last as long as the Ward itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4- M20 has rules for damage over time. HDYDT pg.37 &quot;Walls, Floods, Force-Fields, Etc&quot; has an example where a wall of ice requires 6 successes to deal 6 levels of damage to anyone who touches it, for the entire day (3 suc for duration +3 for damage). Following this logic and the Mage rule where you can heal using the damage chart in the proportion of 2 health levels per success, then a mage can heal 6 levels of damage everytime someone hurts him, for an entire day with 6 successes. </div> </div> </div>In Mage like in most games rules go from the most abstract general rules to the specific rules of each case. While in Mage specific rules won't always trump general ones, one thing that you should try to avoid it's to deduce general rules from specific ones.<br /> <br /> In other words, no. The rule you mention it's specific to barriers, even if the ST deems them kosher they can't be expected to be compatible with the more general rules of healing that can be found in the Basic.<br /> <br /> Unless, perhaps, you craft a &quot;Wall of Healing&quot;, following ALL the rules for &quot;Walls, Floods, Force-Fields, Etc&quot; including the Quintessence costs, location, etc . And even then it's doubtful because this rule you mention it's part of the section about altering forces and elements, not healing or life in general. It's probably not what Satyros had in mind with these rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-28-2018, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T06:48:53-08:00","id":1277348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276791-ritual-questions?p=1277230#post1277230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For your simple but quite unbreakable spells you want the Minor Wards (Correspondence 2+/ Other Spheres) from HDYDT:<br /> <br /> Minor Wards cannot really block anything but they can hold other spells that are automagically triggered when someone crosses the barrier.<br /> <br /> Wards that aren't set on a location but on an object or person have to be &amp;quot;locked&amp;quot; there with the appropiate Pattern Sphere. The level of Correspondence needed it's either equal to the highest Sphere level used in the Ward or 2, whatever it's higher (Similar as when you use Corr to cast at distance).<br /> <br /> A given example it's a Life 3/ Mind 3 effect that gives trespassers a psychic shock when they try to pass the ward. Overt attacks like this one work only once per point of Quintessence expended in the Ritual to create the Ward (and are triggered only once per trespass), but more subtle influences that are always active within the ward (like a house that frigthens trespassers) may last as long as the Ward itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just read minor wards in HDYDT and they doesn't seem to do what you just said. They only subtract successes from the target rolls. There would make no sense in Correspondence doing this kind of thing, since it's a sphere related to space and a ward is just that, changing space to avoid some kind of people to enter/touch/interact within the warded area/object/person.<br /> <br /> Maybe locking effects with pattern spheres would make more sense. Like, in the example of the amulet, locking an effect that makes anyone who touches it besides the mage feel a strong burn. Would require Matter to lock the effect, Forces to burn and mayne Life to identift the patterns as the caster or not...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276791-ritual-questions?p=1277230#post1277230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Mage like in most games rules go from the most abstract general rules to the specific rules of each case. While in Mage specific rules won't always trump general ones, one thing that you should try to avoid it's to deduce general rules from specific ones.<br /> <br /> In other words, no. The rule you mention it's specific to barriers, even if the ST deems them kosher they can't be expected to be compatible with the more general rules of healing that can be found in the Basic.<br /> <br /> Unless, perhaps, you craft a &amp;quot;Wall of Healing&amp;quot;, following ALL the rules for &amp;quot;Walls, Floods, Force-Fields, Etc&amp;quot; including the Quintessence costs, location, etc . And even then it's doubtful because this rule you mention it's part of the section about altering forces and elements, not healing or life in general. It's probably not what Satyros had in mind with these rules</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you're right. What would be the rule to healing with durstion then? What if the mage wants a wolverine constant healing factor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T12:24:38-08:00","id":1279533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276791-ritual-questions?p=1277348#post1277348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just read minor wards in HDYDT and they doesn't seem to do what you just said. They only subtract successes from the target rolls.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but if you read the whole Warding section you may see that it does cover these kind of effects we're talking about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> p.95</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correspondence 2 simply establishes a mage\u2019s influence within a small area. As described under the Correspondence Sphere entry in Mage 20, this Minor<br /> Ward Effect \u201cthickens\u201d the space, <b>and \u2013 when combined with other Spheres as described below \u2013 allows that mage to influence \u201cobjectives\u201d within that area</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, &quot;influence&quot; doesn't say a lot, but let's keep reading...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p.96</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 2 can send \u201cbad vibes\u201d to trespassers, while <b>Mind 3 or Life 3/ Mind 3 can give them a psychic shock if they try to pass the ward</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p.101</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 3, when connected to a ward, can stab the offending party with an invisible knife of psychic pain. <b>If and when the trespasser crosses into the area of the ward, she suffers an immediate bashing-damage attack</b>, as described under Psychic Blast in the Uncanny Influence section...<b>This attack, however, is set into the ward and thus remains invisible when it goes off.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So, Wards can release magical attacks on trespassing acording to HDYDT.<br /> <br /> Altrough there's no actual rule preventing to use any of this in a Minor Ward, one could argue that you need a Major Ward in order to harm someone or cast particularly potent spells (whatever that means), because Minor Wards aren't supposed to cause harm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>99</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor Wards<br /> ... impedes its target in small ways, and <b>although the entity won\u2019t be </b>blocked or <b>harmed directly</b>, its ability to act against the mage is severely limited ...</div> </div> </div> </div>But then extreme pain isn't direct harm, and thus it can act as a deterrent all the same.<br /> <br /> One would think that Time 4 would be necessary for any sort of triggering to happen, however I didn't read anything about Time in this part...But let's see what Time does for Wards just in case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p.97</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A circumstantial ward adds Time 4, plus an event that will trigger the activation of the ward. This sort of ward works only once, but it endures until that event comes to pass. Trigger event examples include: When a red-haired girl opens this door, When the ghost of my father-in-law appears, or When the demon Moliax tries to grab my ass.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p.101</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless secured with Time 4, or otherwise made permanent, any psychic ward lasts for the normal Duration of the Effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time 4 only triggers the Ward itself, and not the effect of the Ward.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There would make no sense in Correspondence doing this kind of thing, since it's a sphere related to space and a ward is just that, changing space to avoid some kind of people to enter/touch/interact within the warded area/object/person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, HDYDT doesn't always make sense, there's no arguing in that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> These rules exist, I'm not inventing anything, but they don't explain quite well how the spell gets delayed or &quot;imbued&quot; into the Ward. Prior to HDYDT I wouldn't have allowed anything of the like w/o Prime 2/3 or Time 4.<br /> <br /> However, there's presedent for Spheres being able to imbue the powers of Rotes upon their respective elements w/o Prime. Life 5 can create a living creature that breathes fire w/o Prime, I wouldn't put past Correspondence to be able to create Wards &quot;that breathe fire&quot; (so to speak).<br /> <br /> It's one of those oddities of HDYDT, albeit not one that I find particularly horrendous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe locking effects with pattern spheres would make more sense. Like, in the example of the amulet, locking an effect that makes anyone who touches it besides the mage feel a strong burn. Would require Matter to lock the effect, Forces to burn and mayne Life to identift the patterns as the caster or not...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that should work too, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the rule to healing with durstion then? What if the mage wants a wolverine constant healing factor?</div> </div> </div> </div>The usual way (well, at least the way Euthanatos do this) with Life 3 it's to create a &quot;bank&quot; of healing that gets expended each time you get hurt. Each succcess allows to heal two Healt Levels, add Duration and during that duration a number of these &quot;banked&quot; successes gets expended to heal you each time you get injured.<br /> <br /> Probably Life 5 can get you a better effect, making &quot;super healing&quot; a power of your own body. This is a Vulgar modification of your Pattern (you will get Permadox), and even then you will have to expend something to heal, probably Quintessence.<br /> <br /> Hence add Prime to suply your Quitessence needs. With Prime 5 you should be able to heal trough breathing the energy of the universe. Hideously Vulgar, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-08-2019, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}